        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cron): preserve on-exit watchers across hot reload",
        "body": "Closes #99709.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where an on-exit cron watched command could be interrupted and re-executed when an unrelated `cron.*` config change triggered gateway hot reload.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nCron hot reload now stops cron scheduling without using the shutdown path that cancels watcher children. The rebuilt cron service reuses the existing watcher manager, refreshes its callbacks, and lets reconciliation cancel only removed or changed jobs.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can edit cron configuration while a watched deploy, migration, or other long-running command is in flight without causing that command to run twice.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/cron-exit-watchers.test.ts src/gateway/server-reload-handlers.test.ts src/gateway/server-cron.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server-cron-lazy.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs src/gateway/cron-exit-watchers.ts src/gateway/server-cron.ts src/gateway/server-reload-handlers.ts src/gateway/cron-exit-watchers.test.ts src/gateway/server-cron.test.ts src/gateway/server-reload-handlers.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n",
        "branch": "fix-cron-exit-watchers-hot-reload",
